  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "R6 and R12 strongly motivate adding Cr to a closely related refractory BCC alloy: they show that Cr promotes Cr-Ta Laves-phase formation and that increasing Cr can strengthen through combined solid-solution and Laves precipitation effects. Other records establish that a continuous ductile BCC matrix with a suitably distributed hard second phase can improve the strength-ductility balance. However, none describes an interconnected reticulated Laves morphology hindering cracks and compensating plasticity; several instead associate Laves or brittle second phases with cracking and ductility loss. Thus the records point clearly toward Cr-induced Laves strengthening, but using a brittle Laves network to increase fracture strain would still require a substantial new microstructural insight."
